In round 57 two prior-work baselines got their third seed, so both now have 3-seed tables, and the 11/06 DAILY is written. Everything is committed and pushed to `r2e/main` (latest commit `2d82067`).

**Results that came in**
- **Park reimplementation, seed 2:** 10-cell success ip 0.98 / pcb **0.02** / pkg 0.64. Over 3 seeds, r2pk beats it on all three board types (paired difference, 95% CI):

  | | ip | pcb | pkg |
  |---|---|---|---|
  | r2pk − Park | +0.10 [+0.05, +0.15] | +0.60 [+0.53, +0.67] | +0.31 [+0.21, +0.39] |

  In the pcb failures, seed 2 fills almost every placeable cell (58–94 decaps) and still misses the target. Seed 1 failed the same way, but only on some problems.
- **Manoharan reimplementation (RL only), seed 2:** ip 0.96 / pcb 0.00 / pkg 0.08.
  - Across 3 seeds: ip 0.96 every time, pcb 0.00 every time (it leaves every port empty), pkg 0.88 / 0.00 / 0.08.
  - r2pk is clearly higher on pcb (+0.92) and pkg (+0.50). On ip the two can't be distinguished (+0.03, CI includes 0).
- Both reimplementations swing a lot between seeds (Park pcb 0.02–0.48, Manoharan pkg 0.00–0.88). The report should only quote seed averages with their range, never a single seed.
- Both RESULTS tables were regenerated by `collect_results.py`. These are report-only comparisons; no verdict rule applies to them.

**Still running**
- GPU: `bp_park_rlonly_s1`. The remaining 4 baseline runs should finish around 07:45 UTC and are evaluated automatically.
- CPU: the local-search run on the 16-cell pcb board `pcb16_0` is 4 h in, expected to finish around 03:00. The other 4 local-search files and 9 scale evals for `r2pk_s2` are queued behind it.
- Pod memory 23.5 / 60 GiB; no new OOM kills.

**Decisions:** no queue or setting changes, because everything is running normally and there are no new instructions or evidence (recorded in PROGRESS). The deadline for starting new fixes is 11/6 12:00 UTC. There is no fix with supporting evidence to try, so no new one will start, and after the baseline runs the GPU stays idle by default.
